# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scraped and derived data
#
# Basketball-Reference is the source for every salary and transaction figure
# here, and nothing in their terms grants us the right to redistribute it. So
# the data does not go in the repo: the *code* that fetches it does, together
# with the manifest saying exactly which URLs were read and when. Anyone can
# rebuild the tables in about six minutes — see "Reproducing the data
# snapshot" in README.md.
#
# This is also why `pip install` of this package is not a way to obtain NBA
# salary data. It is a way to obtain the ingest that fetches it yourself.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw cached HTTP responses (~73 MB of Basketball-Reference HTML).
data_cache/

# Ingested tables: per-player salaries, transaction logs, team payroll sums.
# Regenerated by `python -m mironba.data.ingest.build`.
mironba/data/snapshots/*/contracts.csv
# Per-year contract structure (end year, guarantees, options) from the
# /contracts/ pages. Same rule as every other scraped salary table: the code
# that fetches it ships, the data does not.
mironba/data/snapshots/*/contract_years.csv
mironba/data/snapshots/*/players.csv
mironba/data/snapshots/*/teams.csv
mironba/data/snapshots/*/transactions.csv

# Derived from those tables by `python -m mironba.data.candidates`.
candidate_report.md

# NOTE: snapshot.yaml and sources.csv are deliberately NOT ignored. They are
# our own provenance record — source URL and retrieval date per table, no
# third-party data — and committing them is what makes a rebuild checkable
# against the run that produced the numbers in the README.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.sqlite
*.db
.claude/settings.local.json

# Run artifacts: manifests, event logs, raw completions. Regenerated by any
# run, and they carry raw model output rather than anything reviewable.
runs/*
# ONE reference run is committed so a fresh clone can see a result rather
# than a description of one. A manifest is OUR OWN deterministic output -
# no model call anywhere in it, regenerable in about six seconds - which is
# the same line the archive draws: our outputs may be committed, scraped
# third-party data may not. Every other run stays ignored.
!runs/curry-lakers-2026/
runs/curry-lakers-2026/*
!runs/curry-lakers-2026/manifest.json

# Console transcripts and the bench sequencing marker. The aggregated
# bench-*.json IS committed — it is the evidence for the numbers in the README.
bench-*.log
bench-*.marker
ollama-serve.log
bench-*.pid
branch-*.json
# Same reasoning: the branch fork is linked from the landing page, and the
# file is 6 KB of our own deterministic output.
!branch-lebron-2026.json
league-*.json
delta-error.json

# API keys. Project-local rather than a system environment variable on
# purpose: exporting ANTHROPIC_API_KEY globally makes interactive Claude Code
# flip from the subscription to pay-as-you-go billing without saying so.
# Read only by llm/providers/anthropic.py, never committed.
.secrets/
.secrets.env
archive/rss/poll.log
